  "question": {
    "text": "Consider the following two statements:<br /><br /><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>P</mi></math> : If <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>7</mn></math> is an odd number, then <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>7</mn></math> is divisible by <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>2</mn></math>.<br /><br /><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>Q</mi></math> : If <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>7</mn></math> is a prime number, then <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>7</mn></math> is an odd number.<br /><br />If <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi>V</mi><mn>1</mn></msub></math> is the truth value of the contrapositive of <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>P</mi></math> and <math><msub><mrow><mi>V</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn></mrow></msub></math> is the truth value of contrapositive of <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>Q</mi></math>, then the ordered pair <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfenced separators=\"|\"><mrow><msub><mi>V</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>V</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></mrow></mfenced></math> equals",
    "image": null
  },
